Z||000017||mrfiero||01-06-2001||03:45 AM||||I'm not sure where you are getting your info from, but there are considerably more '88 Fieros with 5-sp. trannies.  The split was almost 50/50......maybe 45/55 in favor of the auto. (more autos.)<P><BR>As far as values go, some people want a fully loaded car and since an auto. tranny was an option over the standard 5-sp. it is desirable to them.  As such they will pay more for it.  I personally don't think the type of tranny on a "collectible" Fiero matters.  It's value has more to do with how many miles it has (the lower the better) and it's condition (i.e. how "new" it is).<P>I paid $10,000 for my '88 GT about 4 years ago.  At the time it had 10K miles (now has 16K) and was nearly flawless.  It was my "dream" Fiero.....black, with tan interior and gold wheels.  It, by the way, is an auto.<P>I also just paid $10,000 for a 5-sp. silver Formula with just over 200 original miles.  This Formula has considerably fewer miles than my GT, but conversely it also has considerably fewer options.  <P>Why did I buy it and why did I pay so much??  Well, it's an '88, it's silver, it was one of the first '88s built (VIN # 01756) and it's virtually brand new.  There were very few silver Fieros built in '88 and I can honestly say that this one has the fewest miles than any other silver Formula (unless I hear otherwise).  That to me makes it collectible, but someone elses idea of collectible may be different.<P>Quite frankly, what a Fiero sells for at a Kruse auction doesn't mean a whole lot to me.  They represent such a small percentage of Fiero sales that it cannot be an accurate gauge for what consitutes "value" and "collectibility".   <P>Just my thoughts on this subject.<P>P.S.  I wouldn't hesitate at plunking down $20K for a fully loaded, super low mileage '88 GT if I had the $$ (and no, I would not drive it!).||||reg||1
Z||000018||fieroparts.com||01-06-2001||08:35 AM||||Well said!<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B> anyone can ask any amt. BUT what they get is what matters. colector cars must be rare <BR>like 5sp v6 was only 10 , 15% of auto numbers in 88 look at kruse auction on line no auto sold for big $$$ even indys . do you know of any sales over 10k for autos   ray </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>1988 GT  000117.1 <BR>Miles T-Tops <BR>Loaded med. red<BR>AS NEW AS THEY GET!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroparts.com</A>  <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fieroparts.com/88gt/88gt117-46.jpg">   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fieroparts.com/mods/88coupe3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
