Z||000022||mrfiero||01-06-2001||07:47 PM||||There were 26,402 Fieros built in '88.  About half of them were 4-cyl. coupes, the other half were divided (almost in half again) into Formulas and GT's.   I don't have exact production numbers for the Formula, but there were 6849 GT's built.  For argument sake, let's say 12,000 Formulas & GT's were built.....at 40% rate for the Getrag vs. auto you would have 4800 with Getrags.    <P>I personaly think that is a low estimate......there is no way only 1500 '88 Fieros came with Getrags.<P>Also, I believe more Formulas had the Getrag than the GT (percentage wise).||||reg||10
Z||000023||Fformula88||01-06-2001||09:36 PM||||Here are the numbers on the 88's<P>4 cyl: 54.3% (13,910)<BR>V6: 45.7% (GT: 6849, Formula: 5643 Tot: 12,492)<P>Transmissions...<BR>5-spd Manual  52.4% (13,835)<BR>3-spd Automatic  47.6%(12,567)<P>Unfortunately I don't have the breakdown of the transmissions between the 4 cyls and V6's, but I'd imagine its not going to be too much different than the overall total.<BR><P>------------------<BR>John<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">    <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
